# Build caches and intermediates — all of these are regenerated by the
# course build scripts, so tracking them only inflates .git.

# build_bedtime.py's per-clip TTS cache. Regenerated from script/*.txt; kept
# at full quality on disk so rebuilds don't re-stitch from lossy input.
# Globbed rather than listed per course: the per-course list silently missed
# every parts-en/ when the English editions arrived, and 483 MB of clip cache
# — more than half again the size of the deployed site — sat staged and one
# commit away from being in this history permanently.
*/data/bedtime/parts/
*/data/bedtime/parts-en/

# The ~400MB PCM intermediate build_bedtime.py mixes from and then deletes.
_narration.wav

# Superseded single-file renders. build_bedtime.py's prior_single_file() carries
# a monolith forward into the next manifest only while it sits beside the
# script, so retiring one means moving it here rather than deleting it: the
# recording survives on disk, the player stops being told it exists.
*/data/bedtime/retired/

# Render logs. Useful while a build is in flight, nothing but weight on Pages.
# The ones committed before this line existed have now been untracked too.
*/data/bedtime/*.log

# fetch_ambience.py's downloaded field recordings and the loops cut from them.
# Build inputs, not site assets — the site serves only the finished mix, and
# ambience/SOURCES.md records where every recording came from.
DSA_tool/data/bedtime/ambience/

# shrink_audio.py's atomic-replace scratch files, if it is interrupted.
*.shrink.tmp.mp3

# API keys. Never commit — .env.example documents the shape instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

__pycache__/
*.pyc

.DS_Store
node_modules/
